  "description": "Three camels are positioned side-by-side in the foreground, all with their heads tilted upward and mouths open as if shouting or laughing. This visual arrangement creates a sense of collective vocalization, which is used metaphorically to represent the 'logic' being mocked in the text. The spatial relationship is one of parallel alignment, with each camel slightly offset from the others, creating a dynamic yet unified composition. The scene is framed against a bright blue sky with scattered clouds, emphasizing the camels as the central focus.",
